  "leProgram": "% Logical English reading of \"Property Policy (sample)\", revision 1, generated by the word authoring POC.\n% Profile wap-le-forms 0.1.0. Not checked by an LE parser.\n\nthe templates are:\n    *a thing* is deemed *a state*.\n    *a party* shall *an activity* within *a period*.\n    *a party* shall not *an activity*.\n    *a party* shall *an activity*.\n    *a party* is not liable for *a matter*.\n    this policy does not cover *a matter*.\n    *a term* means *a description*.\n\nthe knowledge base property_policy includes:\n\n% 1.1 Definition (form definition)\n\u201cInsurer\u201d means the underwriter providing cover under this Policy.\n\n% 1.2 Definition (form definition)\n\u201cInsured\u201d means the person named as insured in the schedule.\n\n% 1.3 Definition (form definition)\n\u201cPremises\u201d means the building described in the schedule.\n\n% 1.4 Definition (form definition)\n\u201cDamage\u201d means physical loss of or damage to the Premises.\n\n% 2.1 Obligation (form obligation)\nInsurer shall indemnify Insured against Damage to the Premises up to the GBP 500,000.\n\n% 3.1 Exclusion (form exclusion-not-cover)\nThis policy does not cover Damage caused by wear and tear.\n\n% 3.2 Exclusion (form exclusion-not-liable)\nInsurer is not liable for the GBP 500 of each claim.\n\n% 4.1 Obligation (form obligation)\nInsured shall take reasonable precautions to prevent Damage.\n\n% 4.2 Prohibition (form prohibition)\nInsured shall not leave the Premises unoccupied for more than 30 days.\n\n% 5.1 Obligation (form obligation-within)\nInsured shall notify Insurer of any Damage within 30 days.\n\n% 5.2 Deeming (form deemed-is)\nA claim is deemed notified on the date Insurer receives written notice.\n",
